(A1 — resizing a global buffer inside a function must keep the reallocated
 pointer in the global BSS mirror so a later direct use sees the new capacity.)

a buffer called buf is 4 bytes in size.

To 'resizeit'.
  Resize buf to 256 bytes.


To 'check'.
  If buf's capacity is equal to 256, print "ok". Otherwise, print "bad".


'resizeit'.
'check'.
